ick launch\"]\n    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Curated notebook tutorials for core journeys\"]\n    E001 --> E004[\"E004 First-pipeline tutorial\"]\n    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Gallery usage and contribution documentation\"]\n    E002 --> E005\n    E003 --> E005\n    E004 --> E005\n```\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (`E001 --> E002` = E001 must complete\nbefore E002 starts).\n\nDeliberate non-edge: no dependency between the Dashboard gallery (E002) and the\ntutorial content epics (E003, E004). The gallery code builds against the packaging\nformat (a build-against artifact); the tutorials are runtime content packaged in that\nformat, not artifacts the gallery code builds against. The epics run in parallel;\ntheir coupling is enforced by acceptance criteria (the gallery is verified against\nformat-packaged tutorials; each tutorial is validated via its packaging manifest).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 12/13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery code builds against the tutorial packaging format — it reads tutorial metadata and pinned images to render and launch. A format/schema is a build-against artifact (API-equivalent), not a configuration reference. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Notebook tutorials are packaged, versioned, and validated per the format; authoring against an undefined format would duplicate and risk rework. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the same format. |\n| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic; the contribution-process docs describe the packaging format itself. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Usage docs describe the built gallery and launch mechanics. |\n| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution docs describe what a curated, tested tutorial looks like. |\n| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution docs cover pipeline tutorials as well as notebook tutorials. |\n\nEpic boundary rationale (Step 5 rules 1-2):\n\n- E002 vs E003/E004: different components and teams (Dashboard/RHOAI Dashboard vs\n  Notebooks/Workbenches and Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines) → separate epics.\n- E001 vs E003: same component and team (Notebooks/Workbenches) but different logical\n  changes and work-product types — defining a packaging/validation format vs authoring\n  tutorial content — with different review criteria → separate epics.\n- E003 vs E004: different components and teams (Notebooks vs Data Science Pipelines);\n  the first-pipeline tutorial is authored as importable pipeline content reviewed by\n  the pipelines team, a different review cycle from notebook content → separate epics.\n- E005: documentation is a distinct work-product type and the strategy lists\n  Documentation as an affected component → separate docs-authoring epic. Content\n  authoring of the tutorials themselves is NOT folded into it — tutorials are curated\n  examples, a different work stream from Red Hat docs topics.\n- HLR-4 is P2 but E005 is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n  frontmatter priority Major → P1); docs-authoring epics do not push priority upstream.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Gallery and one-click launch mechanics (workbench notebook or pipeline import). |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | The six curated tutorials split by component: five notebook journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) in E003; the first-pipeline tutorial in E004. Both epics are P0; neither is deferrable — HLR-2 requires all six. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Priority raised P1 → P0 by inheritance: E001 transitively enables HLR-1 and HLR-2 (all P0 work). See Health Warnings. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 