{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc5315c811aea9a0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# RHAISTRAT-9019 Decomposition — Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery, priority Major).\n13\t\n14\tTriage: NOT below-threshold and NOT docs-only. The strategy's own problem statement\n15\tidentifies three distinct work streams with different owners and review processes —\n16\tproduct code (Dashboard gallery and launch mechanics), authored content (the tutorials\n17\tthemselves: notebooks and pipelines), and documentation — spanning four components\n18\t(Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines, Documentation). The multiple-distinct-\n19\twork-streams escape condition applies, so a full multi-epic decomposition was produced.\n20\t\n21\t## Epic List\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n24\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 (inherited from P1 HLR-3, see Health Warnings) |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Curated notebook tutorials for core journeys | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | First-pipeline tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHAI Documentation | P1 (docs-authoring exception: strategy priority Major → P1) |\n30\t\n31\t## Dependency DAG\n32\t\n33\t```mermaid\n34\tgraph TD\n35\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\"] --> E002[\"E002 Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch\"]\n36\t    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Curated notebook tutorials for core journeys\"]\n37\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 First-pipeline tutorial\"]\n38\t    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Gallery usage and contribution documentation\"]\n39\t    E002 --> E005\n40\t    E003 --> E005\n41\t    E004 --> E005\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tArrows point from dependency to dependent (`E001 --> E002` = E001 must complete\n45\tbefore E002 starts).\n46\t\n47\tDeliberate non-edge: no dependency between the Dashboard gallery (E002) and the\n48\ttutorial content epics (E003, E004). The gallery code builds against the packaging\n49\tformat (a build-against artifact); the tutorials are runtime content packaged in that\n50\tformat, not artifacts the gallery code builds against. The epics run in parallel;\n51\ttheir coupling is enforced by acceptance criteria (the gallery is verified against\n52\tformat-packaged tutorials; each tutorial is validated via its packaging manifest).\n53\t\n54\t## DAG Justification\n55\t\n56\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n57\t|------|------|-----------|\n58\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 12/13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery code builds against the tutorial packaging format — it reads tutorial metadata and pinned images to render and launch. A format/schema is a build-against artifact (API-equivalent), not a configuration reference. |\n59\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Notebook tutorials are packaged, versioned, and validated per the format; authoring against an undefined format would duplicate and risk rework. |\n60\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the same format. |\n61\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic; the contribution-process docs describe the packaging format itself. |\n62\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Usage docs describe the built gallery and launch mechanics. |\n63\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution docs describe what a curated, tested tutorial looks like. |\n64\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution docs cover pipeline tutorials as well as notebook tutorials. |\n65\t\n66\tEpic boundary rationale (Step 5 rules 1-2):\n67\t\n68\t- E002 vs E003/E004: different components and teams (Dashboard/RHOAI Dashboard vs\n69\t  Notebooks/Workbenches and Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines) → separate epics.\n70\t- E001 vs E003: same component and team (Notebooks/Workbenches) but different logical\n71\t  changes and work-product types — defining a packaging/validation format vs authoring\n72\t  tutorial content — with different review criteria → separate epics.\n73\t- E003 vs E004: different components and teams (Notebooks vs Data Science Pipelines);\n74\t  the first-pipeline tutorial is authored as importable pipeline content reviewed by\n75\t  the pipelines team, a different review cycle from notebook content → separate epics.\n76\t- E005: documentation is a distinct work-product type and the strategy lists\n77\t  Documentation as an affected component → separate docs-authoring epic. Content\n78\t  authoring of the tutorials themselves is NOT folded into it — tutorials are curated\n79\t  examples, a different work stream from Red Hat docs topics.\n80\t- HLR-4 is P2 but E005 is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n81\t  frontmatter priority Major → P1); docs-authoring epics do not push priority upstream.\n82\t\n83\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n84\t\n85\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n86\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n87\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Gallery and one-click launch mechanics (workbench notebook or pipeline import). |\n88\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | The six curated tutorials split by component: five notebook journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) in E003; the first-pipeline tutorial in E004. Both epics are P0; neither is deferrable — HLR-2 requires all six. |\n89\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Priority raised P1 → P0 by inheritance: E001 transitively enables HLR-1 and HLR-2 (all P0 work). See Health Warnings. |\n90\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | docs-authoring priority exception: strategy priority Major → P1. |\n91\t\n92\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n93\t\n94\t## Health Warnings\n95\t\n96\t1. **Priority inversion (HLR-3, P1 → E001 P0).** The strategy labels the tutorial\n97\t   packaging format P1, but the format is a prerequisite of both P0 HLRs: the gallery\n98\t   builds against it and every tutorial is packaged and validated per it. By the\n99\t   priority-inheritance rule (an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0), E001 is\n100\t   set to P0. Human verification recommended: if the strategy authors intended the\n101\t   gallery and tutorials to ship WITHOUT the independently-versioned packaging format\n102\t   (e.g. tutorials bundled with Dashboard releases as a stopgap), the E001 → E002 /\n103\t   E003 / E004 edges should be revisited and E001 returned to P1 — that is a product\n104\t   sequencing decision the strategy text does not settle.\n105\t2. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n106\t   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no non-functional\n107\t   requirements; Affected Components is a bare list without change/owner columns.\n108\t   Teams were taken from `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams (Dashboard →\n109\t   RHOAI Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI\n110\t   Pipelines). Documentation has no architecture-context file, so its team\n111\t   (\"RHAI Documentation\") is inferred. Epic acceptance criteria below are derived\n112\t   from HLR text rather than strategy ACs.\n113\t3. **Epic size over the ~2-week guideline (E003).** Estimate: five authored, curated,\n114\t   release-tested notebook tutorials in one epic — plausibly at or above the ~2-week\n115\t   epic guideline (the strategy provides no effort arithmetic). Kept whole because\n116\t   the five tutorials form one curated, jointly-tested content set sharing the\n117\t   packaging format, authoring workflow, and review cycle; splitting would fragment\n118\t   one content stream and duplicate the shared setup/validation work per fragment.\n119\t   Re-split trigger: if authoring+testing of the set runs past the ~2-week guideline\n120\t   (measurably: more than two tutorials still untested at the end of the second\n121\t   week), split E003 by journey group (e.g. data/workbench tutorials vs\n122\t   training/deployment/RAG tutorials) into separate content epics.\n123\t4. **Component mapping notes (non-obvious mappings).** E001 (packaging format) spans\n124\t   tutorial content across Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines; it is assigned the\n125\t   single most-relevant canonical name \"Notebooks\" because the majority of tutorial\n126\t   content is notebooks and the pinned images it specifies are workbench images\n127\t   maintained in the Notebooks domain. The \"first deployment\" tutorial is treated as\n128\t   notebook content (E003, Notebooks) — Serving Runtimes is not an affected component\n129\t   and the tutorial demonstrates the journey from a notebook. E004 is the only epic\n130\t   mapped to Data Science Pipelines (importable pipeline-DSL tutorial content).\n131\t5. **Out-of-scope boundary respected.** Partner/community tutorial intake tooling and\n132\t   localization are out of scope per the strategy; the contribution process is\n133\t   documented (E005) but no submission tooling is built.\n134\t\n135\t## Tiered Delivery\n136\t\n137\tNot applicable — the strategy declares no external dependencies with uncertain\n138\ttiming (no dependencies table, \"Open Questions: None\"), so no Tier 1/Tier 2 split\n139\tis needed. All epics are internal to the platform teams.\n140\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-875930423f746ab9","agent_id":"ada5988a28cfc52e5","session_id":"6f9618b5-3632-482b-87dd-54640f671069","uuid":"d47b9663-413d-437a-98ad-b2c5d7fbc5b6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:40:24.054Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc5315c811aea9a0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
