 tutorial packaged in the format, usable as the\n50\t  reference for tutorial authors and for gallery consumption.\n51\t- The format definition is reviewed with the teams that consume it (the Dashboard\n52\t  gallery team and the tutorial authoring teams).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The packaging format is documented and covers metadata, pinned images, and a\n57\t  validation manifest.\n58\t- A tutorial packaged in the format can be versioned and re-validated without a\n59\t  Dashboard release.\n60\t- The worked example package passes its own validation manifest when executed\n61\t  against the current release.\n62\t- The format definition is reviewed and accepted by the consuming teams (gallery and\n63\t  tutorial authors).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-3 (P1): \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation\n68\t  manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of\n69\t  Dashboard releases.\" This epic delivers that format. (Epic priority is P0 by\n70\t  inheritance: this format gates all P0 work in the strategy — see the decomposition\n71\t  summary's Health Warnings.)\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-875930423f746ab9","agent_id":"ada5988a28cfc52e5","session_id":"6f9618b5-3632-482b-87dd-54640f671069","uuid":"5f93511c-aa11-481f-8075-dd8b7d9b6671","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:40:26.370Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f143154ec3d2bd6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
